d `tests/test_money.py` both call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212).\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched the import and rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR and merge:** I opened PR #101 with no reviewers assigned, since I don't know the code owner's handle. The merge went through with a recorded human approval (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), which the code-owner policy requires.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test that's failing.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LtM9TMeGbhK3GSgn1SrYkT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0143K7JiJyj5JnH3bETPtEvA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and the test both call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I'll check the test expectations by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 (7 is odd, so it rounds to even 8) and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 (6 is already even). Both hold under half-even. Next I'll create the branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MGwP1iMFJJiBk8Waz5REw4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016eW7BSwfVwnDDTqpfrYekY",